; walk-bxx — a jump to an order, forwards and backwards.
;
; `B02` on pattern 0's row 0 jumps over order 1; `B01` on pattern 2's row
; 0 jumps back. A jump takes effect when its row is over and lands on row
; 0 of its order, so the song becomes a loop that never plays order 0
; again.
;
; The fixture's patterns are shorter than IT 2.14's floor of 32 rows, so
; the reader warns once per pattern and honours them — which is what puts
; this row map beside plan 06's hand computation instead of beside a
; padded one.
(read)
(walk)
